# Data directories — ignore the entire data/ tree.
# The old form (data/<sub>/*) only matched the four canonical subdirs, so sibling
# snapshot dirs like data/curated.pre-rerun-2026-06-28/ leaked as untracked (1.5 GB
# risk during commits). `data/` ignores the whole tree. The four
# data/{raw,staging,curated,reports}/.gitkeep markers are ALREADY tracked and stay
# tracked (git ignore rules never untrack), so the dir structure survives a fresh clone.
data/
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.feather

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.egg

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Testing
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ML/NLP artifacts
*.bin
*.pt
*.onnx
models_cache/
embeddings_cache/
faiss_index/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Hypothesis property-test cache (machine-local; never commit)
.hypothesis/

.claude/.consulted/
.claude/.librarian-consulted/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scratch/

# Generated structural ontology index (main#939 child rollout da#405, #820 C×T2).
# The structural layer is "always-current-by-regeneration" (#857) — regenerated
# wholesale from source by the owned generator (ontology_gen in noorinalabs-main,
# via `python3 scripts/structural_ontology.py emit`). Committing it made EVERY
# concurrent PR that touched any source file conflict on a whole-file generated
# artifact that carries no information (the only correct resolution is "discard
# both, regenerate"), and GitHub's server-side merge cannot run the per-clone union
# merge-driver that tried to paper over it. So it is no longer committed: it is a
# build product, produced on demand and read locally. noorinalabs-main's cross-repo
# aggregator (ontology_gen.aggregate) regenerates this repo's index locally before
# rolling up, so nothing depends on a committed copy. See issue da#405 / main#939.
ontology/structural/
